Spike complete — report-only. Decision recorded in `docs/plan/phases/phase-06-report.md` (new phase file) and `.ralph-tui/progress.md`.

**Decision:** model folders as a `driveFolder` app object (`name`, `parent` self-relation tree, color/icon, `position`) plus an **additive `folderId` MANY_TO_ONE relation on the standard `attachment` object** (inverse `files`, `SET_NULL`) — not a new target on the attachment `targetMorphId` morph set. Rationale: the morph set means "record this file is attached to"; folder is an orthogonal, view-filterable organizational axis that coexists with any morph target, is additive-only, and carries no server/morph blast radius. `folderId`/`sourceApp` are attribution, not permission (C5).

**Recorded:** existing primitives (7 morph targets sharing one morphId, FILES field/`FileEntity`/`FileFolder.FilesField`, native Files upload path), the P3 documents attachment pattern, limitations (`folderId` only organizes `attachment` records, not arbitrary FILES-field/rich-text files — project over both, no second file system), and the honest P6 gate (P0.2/P0.4 `[x]`; P1.7a still `[~]`, waiting on P1.6c).

